r body is under 10%, so I coded it `near-unanimous`. On its own it cannot carry a chair.\n- **Bill text:** the operative section bars schools from keeping a student's education record from parents. It also bars changes to that record about gender identity made \"without written parental consent\". This rules out rungs 1 and 2, so it shows a side. But the thing it acts on is the education record. Rung 5 is about staff using a different name or pronouns, and rung 3 is about telling parents when they ask; the bill matches every clause of neither (H17). I coded it `direction-only`.\n\nI listed one gap in `needs_source`: Whyte's own words on whether schools must tell parents about a student's name or gender identity change. The row has no candidate quotes.","ttft_ms":11697,"type":"result","duration_ms":26114,"uuid":"a8f53f15-c7cb-418f-9b22-4eba14d8b36f","ttft_stream_ms":1484,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":1484,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
